      "content": "Hypertension, or high blood pressure, is when your blood pushes too hard against your artery walls. It can cause big health problems like heart disease, stroke, and kidney issues. To manage it, you can change your lifestyle. Eat healthy, exercise, and avoid smoking and too much alcohol. Medicines might also help. Work with your doctor to keep your blood pressure in check and lower your risk of health problems.",
